From: Ahmed Adel Wafdy <fandes99@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tcp_driver): build with Boost 1.87 and later

Boost 1.87 removed ip::address::from_string(), io_context::post(),
io_context::run(error_code &) and basic_waitable_timer::expires_from_now().
Boost 1.89 stopped including the deprecated deadline_timer from
boost/asio.hpp, and Boost 1.90 warns on it, which would break consumers
of the installed tcp_socket.hpp that build with -Werror.

Use ip::make_address(), boost::asio::post(), expires_after() and, like
HttpClient already does, a steady_timer for the connect deadline. A
monotonic clock also keeps the 5 s timeout from jumping when the system
clock is stepped. All of these exist since Boost 1.66.

TcpDriver::run() keeps returning an error_code: run() throws
boost::system::system_error where run(ec) set ec. One difference: a
system_error thrown by a completion handler is now returned too, where
it used to propagate.

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/autowarefoundation/transport_drivers/pull/6]
Signed-off-by: Ahmed Adel Wafdy <fandes99@gmail.com>
